GET my-index/_search
{
"query": {
"match": {
"description": "gelato"
}
}
}
In this case, OpenSearch returns the following response:
{
"hits": {
"total": {
"value": 1,
"relation": "eq"
},
"max_score": 0.99463606,
"hits": [{
"_index": "my-index",
"_type": "_doc",
"_id": "1",
"_score": 0.99463606,
"_source": {
"description": "ice cream"
}
}]
}
}
Tip
Dictionary ﬁles use Java heap space proportional to their size. For example, a 2 GiB
dictionary ﬁle might consume 2 GiB of heap space on a node. If you use large ﬁles,
ensure that your nodes have enough heap space to accommodate them. Monitor the
JVMMemoryPressure metric, and scale your cluster as necessary.
